WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.294
Use the evidence router as a professional habit.

2
00:00:03.294 --> 00:00:08.511
A RISC-V specification proves architectural behavior, not the CVA6 pipeline.

3
00:00:08.511 --> 00:00:12.560
The charter proves governance, not that a branch passes CI.

4
00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:16.952
A TAC roadmap expresses direction, not that planned RTL shipped.

5
00:00:16.952 --> 00:00:22.924
A CVA6 repository exposes code and releases, but does not define all RISC-V processors.

6
00:00:22.924 --> 00:00:25.738
A CVE2 manual is implementation-specific.

7
00:00:25.738 --> 00:00:30.542
CORE-V-VERIF shows a verification environment, not universal coverage.

8
00:00:30.542 --> 00:00:33.150
Match every claim to the source scope.

